# TEMPLATE for the PRIVATE overlay repository (fictional; docs/private-overlay.md "Branch
# protection").  Replace @lab-owner-fake with your GitHub user (or a team).  With "Require review
# from Code Owners" on main's branch protection, a pull request that changes how the lab is
# checked or deployed needs the owner's approval: the required `checks` job runs the workflow
# from the pull request itself, so without this a pull request could rewrite checks.yml to pass.
# While you are the only writer, GitHub cannot let you approve your own pull request: merge as
# admin (the rule binds everyone else) and turn the bypass off when a second writer joins.

# the workflows, and this file
/.github/                     @lab-owner-fake
# what the deploy runs, with what tools, and the runner's job-started hook
/bin/                         @lab-owner-fake
/runner/                      @lab-owner-fake
/ansible.cfg                  @lab-owner-fake
/ansible/playbooks/           @lab-owner-fake
/locks/                       @lab-owner-fake
# what the lab claims as its own: the site's delegated IPv6 prefixes (a model runtime's lab-only
# rule trusts them), its zones and its scope
/lab/site.yml                 @lab-owner-fake
# what must be sealed, and to whom
/.sops.yaml                   @lab-owner-fake
/.hnx-private-overlay.yml     @lab-owner-fake
